From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 15:44:27 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 45/46] flashnext: split fn_row_best over 32 blocks a row for
 the MTP rows

fn_row_best runs one 1024-thread block per row, so a one-row draft step
fills one SM for about 30 us. fn_row_best_max and fn_row_best_sum do the
same two passes over (row, warp) blocks of 32 threads: each thread reads
the same strided values and each warp does the same shuffles, so the
best, its first id and the log-sum-exp keep their bits. The row's last
block (an atomic ticket) folds the 32 warp sums as warp 0 did.

Head.best uses the split for rows up to round_rows; the contract test
checks the split output byte for byte against fn_row_best.
